        "problem": "If $\\overset{\u2015}{R}={m,a,t,h,s}$ and $\\overset{\u2015}{S}={s,e,t},$ then what is $\\overset{\u2015}{R\\cup S}?$",
        "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{R\\cup S}\u2261\\overset{\u2015}{R}\\cap \\overset{\u2015}{S}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{R\\cup S} & =\\overset{\u2015}{R}\\cap \\overset{\u2015}{S} \\\\  & ={m,a,t,h,s}\\cap {s,e,t} \\\\  & ={s,t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
